python3 main.py --problem_name MRFCompress-3 --data_csv ./data/MRFCompress-3/train.csv --llm_config llm.config --background "Find the mathematical function skeleton that represents magnetorheological effect in compress mode, given data on lambda12(L1/L2), lambda23(L2/L3), and alpha(the parameter that controls the surface curvature of the particles). L1, L2, and L3 are the long axis, medium axis, and short axis of the cuboid bounding of superellipse particle. The superellipsoid equation was selected as the construction constraint equation: \left(\frac{x}{L_1}\right)^{\frac{2}{\alpha}} + \left(\frac{y}{L_2}\right)^{\frac{2}{\alpha}} + \left(\frac{z}{L_3}\right)^{\frac{2}{\alpha}} = 1"